> a(x: i32, y: i32) = (x*y) xor 5
> b(x: i32, y: i32) = (y*x) xor 5
> equiv a b
a and b are equal on the domain of a (sampled, not proved; SAT gave up on 9326 AIG nodes within its budget of 100000 conflicts or 100000000 steps)
> c(x: i64, y: i64) = x*y
> d(x: i64, y: i64) = y*x
> equiv c d
c and d are equal on the domain of c (proved by algebra: both sides expand to one polynomial in x, y mod 2^64)
